PHP 8.5 / clang aarch64: keep execute_ex out of class-linking callers.

With PGO + ThinLTO, clang 19 can inline execute_ex into zend_do_link_class,
whose dynamic alloca uses x19 as the frame base. A preserve_none opcode call
clobbers x19, and the generated caller does not restore its frame base. Class
linking through an autoload handler then segfaults instead of resolving the class.
Keeping execute_ex out of line avoids that compiler frame-base preservation
failure while retaining the TAILCALL VM and its optimized opcode handlers.

No configure or extension-registry change can target this inlining boundary.
Disabling PGO, ThinLTO or TAILCALL globally would discard working optimizations;
this workaround affects only the executor on clang aarch64. Patch both the
shipped executor and its generator template so regeneration preserves it.
Remove after a toolchain update passes this autoload regression without the
patch, with PGO + ThinLTO on aarch64.

--- a/Zend/zend_vm_execute.h
+++ b/Zend/zend_vm_execute.h
@@ -112693,6 +112693,8 @@
 #if defined(_WIN64) && defined(_M_X64)
 /* See save_xmm_x86_64_ms_masm.asm */
 void execute_ex_real(zend_execute_data *ex)
+#elif defined(__clang__) && defined(__aarch64__)
+ZEND_API zend_never_inline void execute_ex(zend_execute_data *ex)
 #else
 ZEND_API void execute_ex(zend_execute_data *ex)
 #endif
--- a/Zend/zend_vm_execute.skl
+++ b/Zend/zend_vm_execute.skl
@@ -10,6 +10,8 @@
 #if defined(_WIN64) && defined(_M_X64)
 /* See save_xmm_x86_64_ms_masm.asm */
 void {%EXECUTOR_NAME%}_ex_real(zend_execute_data *ex)
+#elif defined(__clang__) && defined(__aarch64__)
+ZEND_API zend_never_inline void {%EXECUTOR_NAME%}_ex(zend_execute_data *ex)
 #else
 ZEND_API void {%EXECUTOR_NAME%}_ex(zend_execute_data *ex)
 #endif
